k37=[0,ct,[0,i,bfW]],k38=eS,k39=[0,b6,[0,i,eS]],k3$="\nPlaces the **statics** refractor on the bindings at the given paths: a GUI type-ascription overlay (offside type cell) for human-readable types on expressions.\nThis does not change program text. If a runtime probe is on the same binding, it is replaced by statics (same transition as the editor\xe2\x80\x99s statics toggle).\nCollapsed definitions are auto-expanded when statics are placed so overlays are visible.\n\nParameters:\npaths: list(string) \xe2\x80\x94 paths to the bindings\n\nSee the system prompt **Projectors and the agent view** for how statics relate to probes and livelits.\n",k4a=[0,[0,k5,[0,R,[0,[0,b6,[0,i,jw]],[0,[0,kh,[0,R,[0,[0,lG,[0,R,[0,owk,owj]]],0]]],[0,[0,hR,[0,g,[0,[0,i,lG],0]]],0]]]]],0],k4b=dP,k4c=[0,ct,[0,i,bhd]],k4d=eS,k4e=[0,b6,[0,i,eS]],k4g="\nRemoves **only** the statics refractor from the bindings at the given paths.\nRuntime probes on the same binding are left unchanged (unlike remove_probe).\n\nParameters:\npaths: list(string) \xe2\x80\x94 paths to the bindings to clear statics overlays from\n",k4h=[0,[0,k5,[0,R,[0,[0,b6,[0,i,jw]],[0,[0,kh,[0,R,[0,[0,lG,[0,R,[0,owm,owl]]],0]]],[0,[0,hR,[0,g,[0,[0,i,lG],0]]],0]]]]],0],k4i=dP,k4j=[0,ct,[0,i,bnb]],k4k=eS,k4l=[0,b6,[0,i,eS]],k4n="\nToggles the statics refractor on or off for the bindings at the given paths (same behavior as the editor statics toggle).\nCollapsed definitions are auto-expanded when statics end up enabled.\n\nParameters:\npaths: list(string) \xe2\x80\x94 paths to the bindings to toggle\n",k4o=[0,[0,k5,[0,R,[0,[0,b6,[0,i,jw]],[0,[0,kh,[0,R,[0,[0,lG,[0,R,[0,owo,own]]],0]]],[0,[0,hR,[0,g,[0,[0,i,lG],0]]],0]]]]],0],k4p=dP,k4q=[0,ct,[0,i,bjz]],k4r=eS,k4s=[0,b6,[0,i,eS]],k4w=[0,0],k4x=[0,0],k4y=[0,1],k4z=[0,1],k4A=[0,1],k4v=[0,E$,[0,bQU,0]],k4u=[0,nm,[0,bd,[0,rK,[0,sR,[0,md,[0,Vi,[0,QK,[0,Pz,0]]]]]]]],k4J=[0,1],k4I=di,k4H=di,k4G=di,k4F=m,k4E=[0,fv],k4D=m,k4C="Printer.add_indent: Not_found",k4K=[0,m],k4L=[0,j7],k4N=[0,"- **checkbox** \xe2\x80\x94 Toggle UI for boolean literals."],k4O=[0,"- **slider** \xe2\x80\x94 Numeric literal editor (integer)."],k4P=[0,"- **sliderf** \xe2\x80\x94 Numeric literal editor (floating-point)."],k4Q=[0,"- **card** \xe2\x80\x94 **Playing-card** editor: a tuple `(Suit, Rank)` such as `(Hearts, Ace)` or a list of those tuples. **Not** for records, modules, or `{ let \xe2\x80\xa6; \xe2\x80\xa6 }` blocks."],k4R=[0,"- **livelit** \xe2\x80\x94 Custom livelit projector for structured literal editing."],k4S=[0,"- **text** \xe2\x80\x94 Multiline string literal editor."],k4T=[0,"- **table** \xe2\x80\x94 Spreadsheet-style editor for a **list of labeled tuples** sharing the same labels; the labels become column headers. Attaches off the **elaborated** form, so it can apply where the surface syntax alone is not yet a table."],k4U=[0,"- **csv** \xe2\x80\x94 CSV **file import** UI. Attaches only when the definition is the **empty list** `[]`; after placement, import fills it with row/tuple syntax. Non-empty lists (e.g. `[1, 2, 3]`) **cannot** take this projector."],k4V=[0,"- **keybinding** \xe2\x80\x94 Key-capture editor for a string literal holding a keyboard shortcut; records the next chord pressed and commits it as the literal."],k4W=[0,"- **color** \xe2\x80\x94 Color picker for an `Oklch(l, c, h)` literal: a swatch plus lightness, chroma and hue sliders. Attaches only to that constructor applied to three float literals."],k4X=[0,0,0],k4Y=[0,m,[0,"These are alternative UIs for literals and structured values that may already appear in code.",0]],k4Z=[0,"### Livelits (menu projectors)",0],k41=[0,m,0],k42=[0,m,[0,"### Syntax projector tools (Filbert)",[0,"`place_syntax_projector(kind, paths)`, `remove_syntax_projector(paths)`, and `toggle_syntax_projector(kind, paths)` apply **syntax projector** UIs to the term selected by each path.",[0,"`kind` must be a menu projector name (`fold`, `slider`, `sliderf`, `check`, `text`, `card`, `csv`, `table`, `livelit`) \xe2\x80\x94 not `probe` or `statics` (those use the probe/statics tools).",[0,m,[0,"**CRITICAL \xe2\x80\x94 livelits are not automatic:** Ordinary Hazel code (`let speed = 50`, `let is_active = true`, list literals, records) renders as **plain text** until you call **`place_syntax_projector`**.",[0,'If the user asks how livelits work, or wants sliders/checkboxes/CSV editors/text boxes, you **must** call `place_syntax_projector` with the right `kind` on each binding path (e.g. `slider` on `"speed"`, `check` on `"is_active"`, `text` on `"message"`, `csv` only when the RHS is `[]`, `card` only on playing-card tuples/lists\xe2\x80\x94see livelit lines above; nested paths like `"config/volume"`).',[0,"**Never** describe interactive widgets as present based only on `insert_*`, `update_*`, or other edit tools \xe2\x80\x94 that is false unless the matching `place_syntax_projector` calls succeeded.",[0,m,0]]]]]]]]],k43=iK(["## Projectors and the agent view",m,"### Fold (`\xe2\x8b\xb1`)","A **fold** is a collapsed definition in the GUI: the definition shows as `\xe2\x8b\xb1` (not source text).","Use `expand` / `collapse` (see **Paths** and **View Tools** above).",m,"### Runtime probe refractor","The **probe** refractor attaches to a binding and shows evaluated values in the agent view (e.g. `expr \xe2\x89\xa1 value`).","Tools: `place_probe`, `remove_probe`, `toggle_probe`.",m,"### Statics refractor (type overlay)","The **statics** refractor shows a type ascription overlay in the GUI (offside type cell) for human clarity.","It does not change program text; the agent\xe2\x80\x99s printed context may not mirror the overlay unless printing is extended.",m]),k44=[0,"**Projectors**: **Folds** display as `\xe2\x8b\xb1` (collapsed defs; expand/collapse in the full prompt).",[0,"**Refractors** overlay bindings: **probes** show runtime values (`\xe2\x89\xa1` in context); **statics** add a type overlay in the GUI.",[0,"**Livelits** are alternate UIs for literals (checkbox, slider/sliderf, text, card, csv, table, livelit, plus fold in the menu).",[0,"**Agent tools**: `place_syntax_projector` / `remove_syntax_projector` / `toggle_syntax_projector` (see full prompt).",[0,"Full detail lives in Filbert\xe2\x80\x99s live system prompt **Projectors and the agent view** section (this excerpt may be truncated).",0]]]]],k4_=[0,m],k49="Editor.Meta.t_of_yojson",k48="Editor.Meta.yojson_of_t",k47="Editor.Meta.t_of_sexp",k45="Editor.Meta.sexp_of_t",k5f=[0,0,[0,1,[0,2,[0,3,0]]]],k5e=[0,0,[0,1,[0,2,[0,3,0]]]],k5g=[0,0,[0,1,[0,2,[0,3,0]]]],k5d=[0,"Empty hole"],k5c=[0,g8],k5b=[0,"Missing operator"],k4$=[0,0,1],k5a=[0,0,0],k5h=[0,[0,k5,[0,R,[0,[0,b6,[0,i,jw]],[0,[0,kh,[0,R,[0,[0,lG,[0,R,[0,owq,owp]]],0]]],[0,[0,hR,[0,g,[0,[0,i,lG],0]]],0]]]]],0],k5i=dP,k5j=[0,ct,[0,i,bmB]],k5k=eS,k5l=[0,b6,[0,i,eS]],k5n=[0,[0,k5,[0,R,[0,[0,b6,[0,i,jw]],[0,[0,kh,[0,R,[0,[0,lG,[0,R,[0,ows,owr]]],0]]],[0,[0,hR,[0,g,[0,[0,i,lG],0]]],0]]]]],0],k5o=dP,k5p=[0,ct,[0,i,bj6]],k5q=eS,k5r=[0,b6,[0,i,eS]],k5t=[0,[0,k5,[0,R,[0,[0,b6,[0,i,jw]],[0,[0,kh,[0,R,[0,[0,lG,[0,R,[0,owu,owt]]],0]]],[0,[0,hR,[0,g,[0,[0,i,lG],0]]],0]]]]],0],k5u=dP,k5v=[0,ct,[0,i,bir]],k5w=eS,k5x=[0,b6,[0,i,eS]],k5M=[0,1],k5J=[0,Lv],k5K=[0,di],k5L=[0,fv],k5H=[0,40],k5G=[0,IY],k5I=m,k5F=[0,0],k5C=[0,j7],k5D=di,k5E=fv,k5z=blf,k5A=dGM,k5B=bY5,k5N=[0,0],k5R=[0,0],k5T=[0,1],k5S=[0,m],k6i=m,k6j="Warning: using backup text! Serialization may be for an older version of Hazel.",k6g="persistence load",k6h="PARSE FAILED (persistence load): loading empty buffer",k6d=[0,1],k6e=[0,0],k6f=[0,0],k6c=m,k5U=[0,[18,[1,[0,[11,d,0],d]],[11,a4,0]],a6],k5V=tL,k5W=[0,[18,[1,[0,0,m]],[2,0,[11,A,[17,[0,a,1,0],0]]]],B],k5X=[0,[3,0,0],aD],k5Y=[0,[17,0,0],y],k5Z=[0,[12,59,[17,[0,a,1,0],0]],C],k50=ahN,k51=[0,[18,[1,[0,0,m]],[2,0,[11,A,[17,[0,a,1,0],0]]]],B],k52=[0,[3,0,0],aD],k53=[0,[17,0,0],y],k54=[0,[17,[0,a,1,0],[12,aI,[17,0,0]]],a7],k6a=ahN,k6b=tL,k5_=ahN,k5$=tL,k58=[0,ahN],k59=[0,tL],k56=ahN,k57=tL,k55=d48,k6k=".*\\)::$",k6l=[0,0],k6q=[0,fv],k6p=[0,0,0],k6o=wP,k6m=m,k